# Qualified operational contexts

- Read `scripts/operations/README.md` before Windows task, SSH, signing, build, or deployment work.
- Distinguish a Codex sandbox denial from a Windows, session, ACL, or network denial.
- For `MonOrdinateur`, do not retry SSH in the sandbox. Use only
  `C:\Windows\System32\OpenSSH\ssh.exe -F %USERPROFILE%\.ssh\monordinateur-pv-mig.conf MonOrdinateur`
  through the exact persistent outside-sandbox approval. Keep strict host checking; never broaden the rule.
- For the local controller task, use the exact approved read-only query
  `C:\Windows\System32\schtasks.exe /Query /TN \MousseControler-HOGP` outside the sandbox.
- Do not request a general SSH, PowerShell, network, or administrator permission.
- Use the qualified scripts in `scripts/operations/`; preserve their structured JSON and exit-code contracts.
- Never infer an interactive display from SSH session 0. Never modify task ACLs or create an elevated helper task.
- HID movement, capture, trust-store changes, MSIX installation, activation, and deployment require an explicit mandate.
- If one capability is unavailable, report the exact boundary and continue independent work.
